From 853b55778e1e5ba7abac5ab7c1976346e1dc25dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Z User <z@container>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 23:36:17 +0000
Subject: [STAGE 1/3] Stage 2: API, business logic & RBAC + migration 0007 ACL
 fix
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds 9 new endpoint groups covering all phase-1 domain objects plus
the agency-scoped audit log reader:

  - GET/POST /api/v1/contacts, GET/PATCH /api/v1/contacts/{id}
  - GET/POST /api/v1/conversations, GET/PATCH /api/v1/conversations/{id}
  - GET/POST /api/v1/messages
  - GET/POST /api/v1/teams, GET/POST /api/v1/teams/{id}/members, DELETE member
  - GET/POST /api/v1/channels, PATCH/DELETE /api/v1/channels/{id}
  - GET/POST /api/v1/kb/categories, GET/POST/PATCH /api/v1/kb/articles
  - GET/POST/PATCH/DELETE /api/v1/canned-responses
  - GET /api/v1/audit-logs (filterable: action, target_type, actor_user_id, since, until)

All list endpoints support offset pagination with hard cap of 100 per page
and return PaginatedResponse[T]{items,total,limit,offset}. All mutations
write a row to audit_logs with action, target_type, target_id, and a JSONB
metadata payload.

RBAC enforced via require_role(...) dependency factory:
  - viewer: read-only everywhere
  - agent: create/update contacts, conversations, messages, KB articles
  - manager: + teams, KB categories, canned responses, channel deletes
  - admin/owner: + channels create/update/delete

Migration 0007 fixes a privilege escalation introduced by 0006's over-broad
grant to m369_login_reader: it now has SELECT only on agencies and
agency_memberships (the two tables the login SECURITY DEFINER function
reads), nothing else. Caught by test_login_reader_has_only_select_on_required_tables.

Adds an SQLAlchemy after_begin event listener on Session that re-issues
SET LOCAL app.tenant_id whenever a new transaction starts, fixing the
"could not refresh instance" failure that occurs when an endpoint commits
mid-request then calls db.refresh(). The tenant_id is stored on
session.info by the get_current_user dependency.

Fixes a bug in the Phase 1 extended models where 6 classes (Message,
MessageAttachment, Channel, KBCategory, KBArticle, CannedResponse)
inherited from mixins only — missing Base — so SQLAlchemy did not
recognize them as declarative. Also fixes AuditLog.metadata_ and
SuperAdminAuditLog.metadata_ to use JSONB (matching the migration) so
dicts can be persisted.

Tests: 25 new integration tests in test_stage2_api_rbac.py covering
cross-tenant IDOR, RBAC role gating, pagination + filtering, audit log
writes, and login_reader ACL regression. All 97 tests pass against real
PostgreSQL 16.2 with real Alembic migrations 0001-0007.

Migration chain: 0001 → 0002 → 0003 → 0004 → 0005 → 0006 → 0007
Total tables: 23 (22 + alembic_version)
Total API endpoints: 41 (up from 14)
Total tests: 97 (up from 72)
